  "notes": "The 12-bar blues is the shape behind loads of rock and roll. Each beat gets two down-strums: the 5 shape, then add your pinky two frets up for the 6, then take it off again. Four bars of A, two of D, two of A, then E, D, A and E to go round again. Great with the drums on."
